# Latin irregular verbs with a built-in present system (`class=`) whose lemma lies outside the
# letters a–d: `sum` and its compounds, `possum`, `prōsum`, `ferō`, `eō`, `volō`, `nōlō`, `mālō`,
# `fīō`, `edō`. Assigned to the a–d author (AUTHORING.md §2). Compounds with a–d lemmas
# (`absum`, `adsum`, `dēsum`, `abeō`, `afferō`, `dō` …) are in verb/<letter>.lex.
# Written from own knowledge (AUTHORING.md §1); format: Heinrich docs/LEXICON_FORMAT_LA.md §5.4.
edō, ēdī, ēsum, edere verb class=edo
eō, iī|īvī, itum, īre verb class=eo intr
ferō, tulī, lātum, ferre verb class=fero
fīō, factus sum, fierī verb class=fio
mālō, māluī, -, mālle verb class=malo
nōlō, nōluī, -, nōlle verb class=nolo
possum, potuī, -, posse verb class=possum
prōsum, prōfuī, prōfutūrus, prōdesse verb class=prosum
sum, fuī, futūrus, esse aux class=sum
volō, voluī, -, velle verb class=volo
